Modifications by satellitedown for Cinference extend MTP draft windows to ten,
use capture-derived CUDA Graph topology classes for MTP profiles, and update
associated round buffers, validation, tests, and documentation. Later
performance changes speed up DFlash2 verification with small-token projection
schedules, a double-buffered K-split FP8 LinearAdd, staged GDN records with
lane-shared reductions, a warp-specialized K8V4 attention kernel with
loader-assisted PV products, evict-first L2 fills for once-read verify weights,
proposal-head and GDN convolution staging, a bank-conflict-free Q4 proposal
head, retuned small-token A8 tiles, a wider argmax, a GDN record convolution
fused into its input projection, a fused RMSNorm-SwiGLU FFN that hands both
NVFP4 projections pre-quantized inputs, a fused query/key RMSNorm-RoPE, a K8V4
verify query prepared once per block instead of in every attention split, a
warp-level proposal top-k merge over L2-resident partials, a staged selector
walk, L2 discards of consumed attention split numerators, a mask-free
softmax path for unmasked K8V4 key tiles, GDN norm-gating CTAs that share x
and weight rows across heads and token tiles, GDN replay records that warm
the next layer's state in L2, a fused RMSNorm E4M3 producer for the FP8
attention input and FFN projections, wide K8V4 verify blocks whose
otherwise idle compute warps accumulate part of the other rows' PV products,
and a K8V4 prompt kernel that pipelines alternating score warp groups and PV
warps across key tiles.
Publication changes add fork branding, provenance and measurement scope,
correct stale range text, make local-path instructions portable, and omit
machine-local agent automation and unrelated sponsorship configuration.
